From ce4c8d31b74adb9d3a52b980c985140fbe37c185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 16:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] ktranslate: surface LLDP management addresses on
 neighbors
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Walks lldpRemManAddrEntry (1.0.8802.1.1.2.1.4.2.1) in addition to the
main lldpRemEntry walk and attaches the first management address seen
for each (timeMark, locPort, remIdx) tuple to the matching neighbor
record. The address is pulled straight from the OID suffix — the table's
index encodes (addrSubtype, addrLen, addrBytes...) — and rendered as an
IPv4 dotted quad, IPv6 colon-hex, or hex fallback depending on the IANA
AddressFamilyNumbers subtype. The walk is best-effort: devices that
don't support the mgmt-addr table still produce neighbor records with
everything else intact.

Adds unit tests for IPv4 / IPv6 / truncated-row handling and an
end-to-end test that parseLLDPNeighbors attaches the address to the
right neighbor via its keying.
---
 pkg/inputs/snmp/metadata/topology.go      | 115 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 pkg/inputs/snmp/metadata/topology_test.go |  66 ++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 173 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

